  "roadmap_item": "v0.22 item 1 -- H-P0, the construction prerequisite",
  "measurement_only": "No handle table is built here, no budget is frozen, no question set is sealed. DESIGN-handles.md §6 orders this census before all three, and B10 makes a handle from outside its coverage red.",
  "headline": "The ingested library is effectively nameless. Of 12777 statements, S-LEX gives a specific handle to 263 (2.06%) and S-INV to 306 (2.39%); their union -- everything a person could plausibly type -- is 417 (3.26%), leaving 12360 statements with no specific handle at all. S-LEX's 263 are exactly the 263 curated statements minus 0: the 12514 lean_workbook statements carry 9 distinct glossary tokens and 6 distinct glossary strings between all of them, and not one of them has a specific S-LEX handle. The naming layer must be built, not indexed.",
  "headline_is_the_stop_clause": "DESIGN-handles.md §9's stop clause fires on specific-handle coverage near the review's indicative ~2%. The review's two indicative numbers are reproduced here exactly -- 263 via S-LEX (review said ~263) and 306 via S-INV (review said ~306) -- so the ~2% figure is confirmed per source, at 2.06% and 2.39%. The typable union is 3.26%, which is the wider reading and is published beside them rather than instead of them. The clause is the design's to adjudicate and the roadmap's to seal; this census's job is to make sure the adjudication has numbers.",
  "specificity_K": 128,
  "specificity_definition": "a handle is specific iff resolves_to_count <= K (DESIGN-handles.md §7 B2). K is NOT re-frozen here; B2 says a re-freeze is argued from the distribution this census publishes, by dated amendment before the table run.",
